" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338752 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338752 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate\n$|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338752 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa886c44-6fbc-583a-a5aa-8d0e7dbb66ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338752 #edb/ref 1074 "The $4$th row of the given matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So, using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+3\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first $3\\times 3$  determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)\\cdot {C}_{21}+2\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-3)+2(1-3) \\\\  & =-5+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the second $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along its $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{31}+1\\cdot {C}_{32}+1\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-2)+(-2+1) \\\\  & =-2+(-1) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-2\\cdot (-9)+3\\cdot (-3)=18-9=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343018 #edb/ref 1080 "-8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|+7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}|" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343018 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343018 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5cf7cfbc-f2b0-5684-bbfc-df2a4dfe1cd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343115 #edb/ref 1080 "-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|-8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}|" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343115 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343115 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6745fcba-99f1-5578-83b5-4b228c41d687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343556 #edb/ref 1080 "-8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}|" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343556 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343556 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "96c34368-3ce8-50f2-93cc-27f082bae5c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343707 #edb/ref 1080 "7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343707 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186343707 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a6f5b999-091a-5e45-b917-5e6ca067d8b4" #edb/ref 175